title: Should "processed" marks be graph data in your skgrepo, or a private server-side store?
pid: e05956e3-27c7-42dc-9009-8f38924cee5b
body: |2-
  As graph data they are committed and the author can see them, as you
  asked; as a store, like the commit-readiness marks, they make no Git
  churn and stay private.
